        "original_id": "6fa2ade7-7727-5850-8e01-a3beee773347",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Shreveport, Louisiana; Red River; Tybee Island, Georgia; Atlantic Ocean\n- Structures: Long–Allen Bridge\n- Roads: U.S. Route 80; Dixie Overland Highway\n- People: Huey Long; Oscar K. Allen\n\nFacts:\n- U.S. Route 80 is an east–west United States Numbered Highway, and much of it was once part of the early auto trail known as the Dixie Overland Highway.\n- The Long–Allen Bridge in Shreveport, Louisiana, opened in 1933.\n- The Long–Allen Bridge is a truss bridge in Shreveport, Louisiana, named for Louisiana governors Huey Long and Oscar K. Allen.\n- The Long–Allen Bridge carries U.S. Route 80 across the Red River.\n- The eastern terminus of U.S. Route 80 is in Tybee Island, Georgia, at the intersection of Butler Avenue, Inlet Avenue, and Tybrisa Street, near the Atlantic Ocean.",
